                <pb facs="0840" n="828" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg828"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.20 Defense (M) Turkey/1021c</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Turkey</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Steinhardt</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-04-17T19:00:00-04:00">April 17, 1944—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>340. Last week British Embassy here submitted memorandum detailing recent and
                    prospective steps being taken by your British colleague with respect to chrome
                    and requested, if Department agreed, that you be similarly instructed.
                    Department replied that you were fully aware of importance attached to chrome
                    and amply authorized to support your British colleague at all times in manner in
                    your joint judgment deemed most effective.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
